 hoped, SCP-5129 shows great promise for treating addiction! I'll notify my superiors of the possibilities. Maybe this can help me squeeze a little more funding out of them. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>TEST 07</strong></p> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Dr. M██████</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> After hearing of the success with D-3740, Dr. M██████ insisted that we cure their overbearance on alcohol, which allegedly has caused much difficulty with their personal relationships.</p> <p><em>I'm wary of using SCP-5129 on foundation personnel at this early stage, but he went over my head on this one. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>Stated Desire:</strong> Alcohol</p> <p><strong>Result:</strong> Subject's desire for alcohol went unchanged. Instead, they lost all drive or motivation to work or continue their research.</p> <p>[Expletive Removed] <em>idiot. I told him we needed to do more testing to make sure there were no risks, but nooooo. Still, I suppose I should be thankful, this told us a lot. If what you think your greatest desire is differs from what it actually is, SCP-5129 removes your actual one. Or more eloquently, it listens to your subconscious over your conscious mind. Dr. M██████ was always very dedicated to his work- I suppose that consumed his mind more strongly than his addiction. This does put a crimp in the practical applications of SCP-5129 though; we don't want to risk removing the wrong thing. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>TEST 16</strong></p> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> D-3715</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> Subject has been deprived of food for two days leading up to this test.</p> <p><strong>Stated Desire:</strong> Food</p> <p><strong>Result:</strong> Subject continued to have a strong urge to sate their hunger. Upon questioning, it was revealed that they no longer had any wish to start a family, something they'd dreamt about for a considerable time.</p> <p><em>So immediate survival needs do not override base desires. Got it. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>TEST 17</strong></p> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Former Dr. M██████</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> <em>Well this is grim. They're making me run tests on my ex-colleague now. I only hope this won't end up being me a few years down the line. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>Stated Desire:</strong> Alcohol</p> <p><strong>Result:</strong> Subject lost desire for alcohol.</p> <p><em>Well there's a relief. This is the first time we've used it more than once on the same person. According to the interview logs, the priest we took this from said only to use it once per person. Everything seemed to go alright though, although the tingling phase took considerably longer this time, almost 70 minutes. I wonder how many times it can be done on the same person. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>TEST 18</strong></p> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Former Dr. M██████</p> <p><strong>Stated Desire:</strong> A romantic partner</p> <p><strong>Result:</strong> After only 10 minutes, subject experienced severe brain hemorrhaging, dying shortly after.</p> <p><em>That answers that. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>TEST 19</strong></p> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> D-3721</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> Subject suffers from eating disorder</p> <p><strong>Stated Desire:</strong> Food</p> <p><strong>Result:</strong> Subject lost most desire for food. While they still eat to nourish themselves, they will only eat the minimum of what they need to stay healthy, and have no particular care for flavor.</p> <p><em>Finally able to get back to this line of testing. It seems SCP-5129 will still leave survival instincts intact. Good to know, that's one less way things can go wrong. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>TEST 20</strong></p> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> D-3721</p> <p><strong>Stated Desire:</strong> Freedom</p> <p><strong>Result:</strong> Subject experienced similar negative effects as in Test 18, as well as experiencing a ███████ of the █████ and ███████████.</p> <p><em>Well that was horrific. But this was only the second test&#8230; maybe there's some neurological factor which determines resistance to repeat usage of SCP-5129? It would be prohibitively costly to find out, especially given the meager benefits. Besides, I don't exactly want to have to witness that ever again. We'll just assume it's a gamble whether it works or not on repeat rituals, and stick to one ritual per person from now on. -Dr. E████</em></p> <p><strong>Summary of Testing:</strong> After completing Test 50, I'm finally approving SCP-5129 for general use among personnel. If you do need to use it, please don't try and throw your psych exams. Some of our desires can be pretty important to how we function. If the evaluator says no, that means NO. -Dr. E████</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-513488-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. This voice always speaks in the first or preferred language of SCP-5129-1</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-513488-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. After experiencing this, one D-Class personnel who self-identified as Buddhist suggested that it was a method for detaching from the material world to reach enlightenment. To them, SCP-5129's question &quot;Do you wish to emerge&quot; was referring to this transition. Further testing has neither confirmed nor denied this theory.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-513488-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. The Priest stated that only holy water would activate SCP-5129. Further investigation confirmed that this belief stemmed from the fact that he collected water intended to be blessed from rainfall, while all his other water was drawn from an artificial well.</div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5128">SCP-5128</a> | SCP-5129 | <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5130">SCP-5130</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ksforshort" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6367089&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609772998" alt="KSforShort" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6367089)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ksforshort" >KSforShort</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
